        else
          # GitHub #38 investigation, second and deeper bug found: a
          # bare integer LITERAL exceeding this backend's 48-bit signed
          # fixnum range (+-140737488355327) was ALWAYS emitted as a
          # raw untagged `mov rax, <literal>` regardless of magnitude
          # -- no promotion ever happens for a literal that's already
          # "too big" from the moment it's created (promotion only
          # ever triggers on ARITHMETIC overflow, detected after an
          # operation). Such a value then matches NEITHER "genuine
          # fixnum" (fails the round-trip test) NOR "real tagged
          # BigInt" (its family nibble is 0, since it was never
          # actually tagged) in any downstream dynamic dispatch --
          # confirmed exactly: `123456789012345 + 987654321098765`
          # (987654321098765 needs 50 bits, already past the 48-bit
          # boundary as a bare literal) silently gave `0`, having
          # fallen through `x64_binop_asm_dynamic`'s `DYN_OBJ_` catch-
          # all (neither a valid fixnum nor a recognized tag) to its
