          # `rt_bigint_from_i64`) the moment it's constructed, so every
          # value reaching arithmetic is either a genuine <=48-bit
          # fixnum or a properly tagged BigInt -- restoring the
          # invariant the rest of this backend's tagging scheme already
          # assumes. `to_num` here parses on the COMPILER's own host
          # side (a real, full-precision number), not the TARGET
          # program's constrained 48-bit representation, so this
          # comparison itself can't overflow.
          # Real bug found and fixed here (same CLASS as the
          # rt_payload_mask fix earlier this session, but a name-prefix
          # exclusion doesn't cover it): x64_runtime.patlang's OWN
          # functions embed large literal constants as RAW BIT
          # PATTERNS (family/tag masks like 1152921504606846976,
